# 17. Distribution Rules

Instead of manually creating every publication task, a system can define distribution rules.

For example:

```text id="4d7xk2"
Campaign: Product Videos

Content Type:
Short Video

Destinations:
Instagram
TikTok
YouTube

Accounts:
Group A

Schedule:
Platform-specific schedule
```

The system can then generate publication tasks automatically.

This separates campaign strategy from individual task execution.

---

# 18. Content Rotation

A content library can contain many assets.

A distribution system can use content rotation to organize which content is assigned to which campaigns.

Conceptually:

```text id="9z4m5n"
Content Library
├── Video 001
├── Video 002
├── Video 003
├── Video 004
└── Video 005
```

The campaign system can then select appropriate assets for individual accounts or destinations.

The exact rotation strategy should be based on the campaign requirements and content policy.

---

# 19. AI in Content Distribution

AI can add another layer to the content pipeline.

Instead of:

```text id="5s0h7x"
Content
 ↓
Publish
```

an AI-assisted system might use:

```text id="k2v6ra"
Content
   ↓
AI Analysis
   ↓
Classification
   ↓
Platform Adaptation
   ↓
Caption / Metadata Generation
   ↓
Human or Automated Review
   ↓
Distribution
```

AI can assist with tasks such as:

* classifying content
* generating captions
* adapting titles
* summarizing videos
* identifying content categories
* selecting suitable formats
* analyzing performance
* recommending distribution strategies

AI should not necessarily control every step.

Deterministic systems are often preferable for operations that require predictable execution.

