# 27. Practical Design Principles

### Treat content as an asset

Separate the content itself from its individual publication jobs.

### Treat publications as independent tasks

Each platform/account combination should have its own state.

### Adapt content when necessary

Do not assume that one format or metadata structure is ideal for every destination.

### Maintain publication history

Know where content has already been distributed.

### Make failures visible

A failed TikTok publication should not obscure successful Instagram and YouTube publications.

### Separate decisions from execution

AI and campaign logic can determine what should happen while workers execute the resulting tasks.

### Monitor the complete pipeline

Content processing, scheduling, publishing, and analytics should all be observable.

